  "definition": "Notification of Emergency Responders",
  "effectiveDate": "2017-09-01",
  "historyNote": "(See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 900) #12364, eff 9-1-17",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Env-Wq 906.01",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq900.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 906.01 Notification of Emergency Responders",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 906.01 Notification of Emergency Responders.\n\n(a) Subject to (d), below, the YRC owner, or designee, shall notify the local police, fire, and rescue departments:\n\n(1) Annually for year-round camps; and\n\n(2) Immediately prior to opening for seasonal camps.\n\n(b) The notification required by (a), above, shall:\n\n(1) Be in writing;\n\n(2) Include the opening and closing dates for seasonal camps; and\n\n(3) Be delivered in hand or sent via private delivery service, U.S. Postal Service, or email.\n\n(c) The YRC owner, or designee, shall:\n\n(1) Retain a paper copy of the notification; and\n\n(2) Provide it upon request to department personnel.\n\n(d) For any YRC located within an area that is served by full-time, non-volunteer emergency response personnel even when the YRC is not in operation, notice as specified in (a), above, shall be required only if requested by the local emergency response agencies.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 900) #12364, eff 9-1-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq900.html"
